  "notes": "Williamson Tea Kenya (WTK on Nairobi Securities Exchange — pseudo-ticker WTK.NR for site naming). Listed on NSE since 1972 (Williamson Tea Kenya Ltd). Kenyan tea producer with 7 estates totaling ~7,000 ha planted tea (~17,300 acres including support land). Fiscal year ends 31 March. Reports semi-annually (interim 6M to Sep + full year to Mar). All figures in KES millions. Pure-play tea — single segment in disclosures (smallholder bought-leaf + estate-grown). Net debt extracted from BS as borrowings less cash. Historical pre-2010 data from NSE archive + Williamson Tea AR archive (some pre-2005 figures only available in print Kenyan annual reports — limited to revenue + net income for those years; balance sheet metrics omitted where unverified). Pre-2008 disclosure followed UK-influenced format inherited from former parent George Williamson plc (delisted 2007). Major restructuring in 2007/08: Williamson Tea Holdings demerged from London-listed parent. Highly volatile annual results due to weather, Kenyan tea auction prices, and KES devaluation effects on USD-denominated tea sales.",
